 ### Thinking Level Map
 
 Use `thinkingLevelMap` on a model to describe model-specific thinking controls. Keys are pi thinking levels: `off`, `minimal`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, `max`. Maps may contain holes; for example, a model can expose `high` and `max` without exposing `xhigh`.
+
+`ultracode` is a harness-only mode rather than a `thinkingLevelMap` key. It is displayed after model levels, sends `xhigh` to the provider (subject to normal model clamping), and lets orchestration extensions activate standing workflow policy.
 
